================================================================================
 1. PREREQUISITES (one-time setup)
================================================================================

1a — Start infrastructure (PostgreSQL, Redis, Coturn):
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d

  This starts 3 containers:
    - anon-chat-db      (PostgreSQL 16, port 5432)
    - anon-chat-redis   (Redis 7, port 6379)
    - anon-chat-coturn  (TURN/STUN server, port 3478)

  Default DB credentials:
    User:     anonuser
    Password: anonpassword
    Database: anondb

1b — Install npm dependencies:
────────────────────────────────
  npm install

  (npm workspaces — all deps hoisted to root node_modules/)

1c — Create backend/.env:
───────────────────────────
  Required file at backend/.env with these values:

    PORT=4000
    DATABASE_URL="postgresql://anonuser:anonpassword@localhost:5432/anondb"
    REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379"
    JWT_SECRET="dev-secret-key-123"
    CLIENT_URL="http://localhost:3000"
    COTURN_SHARED_SECRET="coturn_dev_secret"
    TURN_URL="turn:localhost:3478"
    STUN_URL="stun:localhost:3478"
    GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
    GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""
    GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL="http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/google/callback"
    TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY="1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA"

  NOTES:
    - Google OAuth will NOT work locally (keys left empty).
      Use guest/email login for testing.
    - Turnstile uses test key that allows all requests locally.
    - DB credentials MUST match docker-compose.dev.yml defaults.

1d — Push Prisma schema to database:
─────────────────────────────────────
  cd backend
  npx prisma db push

  (Creates all tables from prisma/schema.prisma)

1e — Seed subscription plans:
───────────────────────────────
  cd backend
  npx tsx prisma/seed.ts

  Creates 3 plans: Daily (29 INR), Weekly (149 INR), Monthly (399 INR)

================================================================================
 2. LOCAL PREVIEW (run each time)
================================================================================

2a — Ensure infrastructure is running:
───────────────────────────────────────
  docker ps  (check anon-chat-db, anon-chat-redis, anon-chat-coturn are UP)
  If not: docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d

2b — Start backend (Terminal 1):
─────────────────────────────────
  cd /home/incognito/Code/anonlink/backend
  npx tsx src/index.ts

  Backend runs on http://localhost:4000
  Hot-reload: NO (unlike nodemon). Stop and restart after changes.
  Alternative: Use nodemon with ts-node if ts-node deps are fixed.
  Health check: curl http://localhost:4000/health

2c — Start frontend (Terminal 2):
──────────────────────────────────
  cd /home/incognito/Code/anonlink/frontend
  npx next dev

  Frontend runs on http://localhost:3000
  Hot-reload: YES (Next.js Turbopack HMR — instant on save)

2d — Preview:
─────────────
  Open http://localhost:3000 in browser.

2e — Stop:
──────────
  Kill both dev servers (Ctrl+C in each terminal).
  To stop infrastructure: docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml down

