 3. IMPORTANT NOTES
================================================================================

3a — Backend dev script issue:
  The configured "dev" script uses "nodemon --watch src --ext ts --exec ts-node src/index.ts"
  but ts-node in backend/node_modules is incomplete due to npm workspaces hoisting.
  Use "npx tsx src/index.ts" directly instead — tsx works correctly.

3b — Frontend env vars:
  NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL defaults to http://localhost:4000 (defined in frontend/src/lib/api.ts)
  NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY defaults to test key (defined in components)
  NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY defaults to test key (defined in components)
  No frontend-specific .env file is required for local dev.

3c — Database state:
  Tables are created via "npx prisma db push" (not migrations).
  No prisma/migrations directory exists.
  Seed script populates subscription_plans table only.

3d — Google OAuth:
  Does NOT work on localhost. Service workers / OAuth redirect URIs
  must be registered in Google Cloud Console for the production domain.
  Test the app using guest login or email/password registration.

3e — Port conflicts:
  Ensure ports 3000 (frontend), 4000 (backend), 5432 (DB), 6379 (Redis),
  3478 (coturn) are free before starting services.

3f — Existing deployment:
  Live server: ubuntu@132.226.190.112 (SSH key at ~/.ssh/anonlink.key)
  Deploy script: ./scripts/deploy.sh [--service frontend|backend|all]
  See AGENTS.md for full deploy workflow.

